// Regression for issue #350: a self-recursive local `fun`, declared inside
// a `try` block and never called. On the JVM backend, the closure's own
// slot goes straight from "never written" to an Object[1] capture cell
// (seedSelfCaptureCell) at the point it declares itself -- and that first
// write used to sit inside the try-protected region. The classic verifier
// that assembles this backend's classes (no StackMapTable) rejects any
// register whose type is not consistent across an entire guarded region,
// including the instructions that run before its first-ever write, so it
// used to reject this class with "VerifyError: Register N contains wrong
// type" even though `f` is never actually called.

try {
    fun f() { return f(); }
    print "declared";
} catch (e) { print "no"; }

// CHECK: declared
